# Fiber Routing & Context API

## Route Definition Patterns

### HTTP Methods

```go
// Standard methods
app.Get("/users", listUsers)           // GET
app.Post("/users", createUser)         // POST
app.Put("/users/:id", updateUser)      // PUT
app.Patch("/users/:id", patchUser)     // PATCH
app.Delete("/users/:id", deleteUser)   // DELETE

// Special methods
app.All("/admin", adminHandler)        // All HTTP methods
app.Add("CUSTOM", "/webhook", handler) // Custom HTTP method
```

---

## Dynamic Parameters

```go
// Named parameters
app.Get("/user/:id", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    id := c.Params("id")
    return c.SendString("User ID: " + id)
})
// Matches: /user/123, /user/abc

// Optional parameters
app.Get("/user/:id?", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    id := c.Params("id", "guest")
    return c.SendString("User: " + id)
})
// Matches: /user/123 AND /user

// Greedy (non-optional)
app.Get("/post/:category+", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    category := c.Params("category") // "tech/golang/fiber"
    return c.SendString("Category: " + category)
})

// Wildcards (optional greedy)
app.Get("/files/*", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    filepath := c.Params("*")
    return c.SendFile("./" + filepath)
})

// Parameters with separators
app.Get("/flights/:from-:to", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.JSON(fiber.Map{
        "from": c.Params("from"),
        "to": c.Params("to"),
    })
})
```

