## Context API - Response Methods

### JSON Response

```go
app.Get("/user", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.JSON(fiber.Map{
        "name":  "John Doe",
        "email": "john@example.com",
    })
})

// With status code (chainable)
app.Post("/user", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.Status(201).JSON(fiber.Map{
        "message": "User created",
    })
})
```

### String Response

```go
app.Get("/hello", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.SendString("Hello, World!")
})

// With status
app.Get("/error", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.Status(404).SendString("Not Found")
})
```

### File Response

```go
app.Get("/download", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // Send file with auto MIME type
    return c.SendFile("./documents/report.pdf")
})

// Trigger download with custom filename
app.Get("/download", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.Download("./documents/report.pdf", "monthly-report.pdf")
})
```

### Redirect

```go
app.Get("/old-path", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // 302 redirect (default)
    return c.Redirect("/new-path")
})

// 301 permanent redirect
app.Get("/old-page", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    return c.Redirect("/new-page", 301)
})
```

### Status Only

```go
app.Delete("/user/:id", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // Delete user...

    // 204 No Content
    return c.SendStatus(204)
})
```

### Set Headers

```go
app.Get("/api", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    c.Set("X-API-Version", "1.0.0")
    c.Set("X-Rate-Limit", "100")

    return c.JSON(fiber.Map{"status": "ok"})
})
```

### Set Cookies

```go
app.Post("/login", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // Simple cookie
    c.Cookie(&fiber.Cookie{
        Name:  "session_id",
        Value: "abc123",
    })

    // Secure cookie
    c.Cookie(&fiber.Cookie{
        Name:     "token",
        Value:    "xyz789",
        Expires:  time.Now().Add(24 * time.Hour),
        HTTPOnly: true,
        Secure:   true,
        SameSite: "Lax",
    })

    return c.SendString("Logged in")
})
```

