## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ DON'T: Add routes dynamically after startup

```go
app := fiber.New()
app.Listen(":8080")

// Later...
app.Get("/dynamic", handler) // ❌ Won't work!
```

**Why**: Routes must be defined before `app.Listen()` for performance.

### ❌ DON'T: Set headers after sending response

```go
app.Get("/api", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    c.JSON(fiber.Map{"status": "ok"})

    c.Set("X-API-Version", "1.0") // ❌ Too late!

    return nil
})
```

---

## Summary

- Use route constraints for validation (`<int>`, `<guid>`, `<regex>`)
- Group related routes for organization
- Use typed query methods (`QueryInt`, `QueryBool`, etc.)
- Parse body once per request
- Use `c.Locals()` for request-scoped data
- Define all routes before `app.Listen()`
